.TH CHAN_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chan_send_zc \- send a message through the channel (blocking)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t chan_send_zc(channel *ch, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Automatically selects the appropriate queue based on calling thread:
- Owner thread sends to owner_to_workers queue
- Worker threads send to workers_to_owner queue

Blocks until space is available and transfers ownership.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to send through
msg  Message to send (data ownership transfers on success)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - Message sent successfully
ccol_invalid_args  - ch or msg is NULL, or msg validation fails
ccol_not_permitted - Sending has been disabled on the selected direction
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Blocks until space is available in the selected queue
Direction is automatically determined by thread ID
On failure, caller retains ownership of msg->data
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chan_try_send_zc (3),
.BR chan_timed_send_zc (3),
.BR chan_recv_zc (3)
